                        ],
                        "form": "журнали́стках"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "46aa766d-78af-3254-904a-02d4cd2e206b",
                        "entry_id": "01f4187f-0896-396a-9e66-be8c300f4dad",
                        "glosses": [
                            "женск. к журналист"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d9f3e584-f20f-41af-9ad0-361d0139eb73",
                                "sense_id": "46aa766d-78af-3254-904a-02d4cd2e206b",
                                "text": "Журналистка одной из центральных газет Австралии приехала к Катарине Причард взять у неё интервью по каким-то вопросам женского движения."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cb7bb4b9-91bb-451b-b7e2-80a254191a73",
                                "sense_id": "46aa766d-78af-3254-904a-02d4cd2e206b",
                                "text": "Тем более что владелицей Резо оказалась журналистка из соседней эстонской газеты ― миловидная Анечка Паю."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "31fd806f-0c8d-4791-b66f-db6e8fd55b61",
                        "source_entry_id": "01f4187f-0896-396a-9e66-be8c300f4dad",
                        "source_sense_id": "46aa766d-78af-3254-904a-02d4cd2e206b",
                        "target_lang_word": "journalist",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "journalist",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b9e3ec57-cbb7-323d-a76b-9fc06b8be575",
                                        "entry_id": "abdaa706-943d-35bc-9a8c-31e5000def8d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The keeper of a personal journal, who writes in it regularly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6b4ff522-11ef-37f0-9ea8-c3b3be58d314",
                                        "entry_id": "abdaa706-943d-35bc-9a8c-31e5000def8d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One whose occupation is journalism, originally only writing in the printed press."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3c767b62-55a2-4dba-aa14-1230c95cbdf3",
                                                "sense_id": "6b4ff522-11ef-37f0-9ea8-c3b3be58d314",
                                                "text": "“There’s this terrible business to start with. Scotland Yard men in and out of the house like a jack-in-the-box! Never know where they won’t turn up next. Screaming headlines in every paper in the country—damn all journalists, I say!”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8ceacc2b-093d-3f74-9e4b-2d5fbf8d07e6",
                                        "entry_id": "abdaa706-943d-35bc-9a8c-31e5000def8d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A reporter, someone who professionally reports on news and current events."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2ef3624b-86a0-47a2-b7b6-3d6b7943b860",
                                                "sense_id": "8ceacc2b-093d-3f74-9e4b-2d5fbf8d07e6",
                                                "text": "British journalists shun complete respectability, feeling a duty to be ready to savage the mighty, or rummage through their bins. Elsewhere in Europe, government contracts and subsidies ensure that press barons will only defy the mighty so far."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "444fff44-ed80-4a6a-ae7a-8a9c64988dd2",
                                                "sense_id": "8ceacc2b-093d-3f74-9e4b-2d5fbf8d07e6",
                                                "text": "A staff member of the Kuchar County Judiciary told RFA that he did not have the authority “to answer political questions of this magnitude,” when asked whether 150 people had died in No. 1 Camp, and whether the number included any government officials or other employees.\n“We have a county-wide directive—firstly, to never provide answers to pretend journalists, and secondly, to never take phone calls of unknown origin,” he said."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b7c03b3a-8b3f-47b7-830c-c19b2962e942",
                                                "sense_id": "8ceacc2b-093d-3f74-9e4b-2d5fbf8d07e6",
                                                "text": "In 2017, Katherine Maher, then the CEO of the WMF, re-imagined the nonprofit’s mission as “top-down social justice activism and advocacy,” as journalist Ashley Rindsberg described it."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a7c8457a-7ac5-49d8-8687-ff0c907d98fc",
                        "source_entry_id": "01f4187f-0896-396a-9e66-be8c300f4dad",
                        "source_sense_id": "46aa766d-78af-3254-904a-02d4cd2e206b",
                        "target_lang_word": "Journalistin",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Journalistin",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "62db2549-6ad3-3753-9006-4acfa16ad9ce",
                                        "entry_id": "50d89d1e-06b9-33c4-9b17-7d47a684b4ac",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Frau, die beruflich für Zeitungen, Zeitschriften oder andere Massenmedien arbeitet und Informationen beschafft und verbreitet"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4eab1331-2220-46c5-b01d-7dbd322a7a6f",
                                                "sense_id": "62db2549-6ad3-3753-9006-4acfa16ad9ce",
                                                "text": "„Sie waren auf Englisch, und schon stellte ich mir eine Zukunft als internationale oder zumindest bilinguale Journalistin vor.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8f56643e-77fc-4ba3-8e36-63db00375f64",
                                                "sense_id": "62db2549-6ad3-3753-9006-4acfa16ad9ce",
                                                "text": "„Als zufällig die Journalistin vorbeikam, zögerte sie zwar, stimmte aber ihrer Bitte nicht ungern zu.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "26ed9ed0-26b5-44a5-a7df-3f01fe1b2f7f",
                                                "sense_id": "62db2549-6ad3-3753-9006-4acfa16ad9ce",
                                                "text": "„Bei einer großen Verlagsweihnachtsfeier unterhalte ich mich mit einer befreundeten Journalistin, und sie kommt auf die Idee, in der Stadtzeitung einen Artikel über den Buchhandel als bedrohte Branche zu schreiben.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b9821177-c38a-4a8b-a0f1-5d68b6d3bd16",
                                                "sense_id": "62db2549-6ad3-3753-9006-4acfa16ad9ce",
                                                "text": "„Für mich als Journalistin waren es mit die schönsten Jahre.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6ae8b540-78c5-476a-abdc-07da295445bb",
                        "source_entry_id": "01f4187f-0896-396a-9e66-be8c300f4dad",
